/-!
# Enactive inference and Bennett weakness

The finiteness-free 2024 theory is primary.  `Enactive.Finite` supplies its
decidable counting model, and `Enactive.Bennett2023` proves that Michael
Timothy Bennett's earlier Boolean-program presentation is an equivalent finite
view preserving statements, extensions, tasks, child structure, and weakness.
The remaining modules compare Bennett's Razor with other selection profiles,
state the exact uniform and credal premises behind its optimality results, and
connect completion freedom to Prime and GSLT structures without identifying
support cardinality with proof multiplicity or task generations with authority
growth.
